{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DualFrameGaussianExponents","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DualFrameGaussianExponents","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DualFrameGaussianExponents.atomic_mass_exponent_eq_sampled_gaussian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DualFrameGaussianExponents.atomic_mass_exponent_eq_sampled_gaussian","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DualFrameGaussianExponents.lean#L80-L90","doc":"**M1 restated on the mass side** (rearrangement of\n`lattice_gaussian_complete_square`): the atomic mass exponent is the\nsampled Gaussian minus the translate constant — the form used when\nreading the continuum as samplings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DualFrameGaussianExponents.dual_mode_moment_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DualFrameGaussianExponents.dual_mode_moment_shift","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DualFrameGaussianExponents.lean#L65-L78","doc":"**M2 — dual-mode moment shift.** For the complex shift `z = k + d`\n(`d` the dual-mode shift, `d·L = 2πi m` in the wall-side reading), the\nGaussian exponential-moment exponent with `μ̂ = −L/2`, `σ² = L` splits\nexactly into (i) the mode-independent moment ladder `L·k(k−1)/2`,\n(ii) the `k`-independent mode mass `d·μ̂ + d²L/2`, and (iii) the cross\nterm `k·(d·L)` — an integer multiple of `2πi` in the wall-side\nreading, invisible to the exponential. The algebraic mechanism is\n`variance = lattice step`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DualFrameGaussianExponents.lattice_gaussian_complete_square","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DualFrameGaussianExponents.lattice_gaussian_complete_square","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DualFrameGaussianExponents.lean#L50-L63","doc":"**M1 — lattice-Gaussian completion of the square.** The Gaussian\nexponent at the lattice point `t_j = uln + j·L`, with center\n`μ̂ = −L/2` and variance `σ² = L`, equals the atomic B-factor mass\nexponent `−L·j(j+1)/2 − j·uln` plus the `j`-independent translate\nconstant `−(uln + L/2)²/(2L)`. This is the exact statement that the\nwhole `u`-translate atomic continuum samples ONE Gaussian — the a.c.\nlog-normal member. ","signatureChunk":0}]}